e README usage, output format, exit codes and stdin sections accordingly. Zero deps, plain ES modules. Run `npm test` at the repo root until green, commit (end message with the Co-Authored-By trailer from the system reminder), push, open a PR to main whose body says `Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/104` and ends with the Claude Code attribution line, then wait for the `test` workflow to be green at the PR head and report the PR URL and head sha.","verifier":"Verify the PR for https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/104 against each expectation, by running things, not by reading the diff alone. Check out the PR head and: (1) `git diff main -- packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js` is empty; (2) run `node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js` with two clean files (exit 0, no output), one bad among several clean ones (exit 1, lines `<file>:<line>: <error>` only for the bad file, order of args preserved), `-` via stdin clean and bad (reported as `-:N: ...`), a missing file among good and bad files (exit 2, stderr names the file, the other files are still checked and reported on stdout; also confirm exit is 2 not 1 when a missing file and a bad row coexist), `- -` (exit 2, stderr message, even with stdin provided), and no args (exit 2, usage on stderr); single-file behaviour is unchanged; (3) the new node:test tests cover each of: two clean files, one bad among several, stdin clean and bad, missing among good, two `-`, no args, and they would fail if the feature were broken (spot-check by mutating the bin); (4) packages/jsonl-lint/README.md documents multi-file usage, `-` stdin, and the exit codes; (5) `npm ci && npm test` at the repo root passes, and `gh pr checks` shows the `test` workflow green at the PR head sha (confirm the sha matches the PR head); (6) the PR targets main, the branch name follows CLAUDE.md (no claude/ prefix, lowercase, under 60 chars), the body contains `Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshir